1️⃣ Start the Lab Environment
lab start cli-health
This prepares the environment and required resources for the exercise.
________________________________________
2️⃣ Login to the OpenShift Cluster
oc login -u admin -p redhatocp https://api.ocp4.example.com:6443
Purpose:
Authenticates you to the OpenShift cluster as an admin user.
________________________________________
3️⃣ Check Installed Operators
Operators manage applications and cluster components.
List user-installed operators
oc get operators
Example:
lvms-operator.openshift-storage
metallb-operator.metallb-system
List default cluster operators
oc get clusteroperators
Important fields:
Field	Meaning
AVAILABLE	Operator working
PROGRESSING	Updating or installing
DEGRADED	Something is wrong
Healthy cluster usually shows:
AVAILABLE=True
PROGRESSING=False
DEGRADED=False
________________________________________
4️⃣ Get Detailed Operator Information
Example:
oc describe clusteroperators openshift-apiserver
This shows:
•	status conditions
•	related objects
•	version
•	events
Important section:
Conditions:
Type: Degraded
Status: False
Message: All is well
Meaning → operator is healthy
________________________________________
5️⃣ Check Pods of the Operator
List pods in namespace:
oc get pods -n openshift-apiserver-operator
Example:
openshift-apiserver-operator-85fc9669d-g58sl
Get detailed status using JSON:
oc get pod <pod-name> -n openshift-apiserver-operator -o json | jq .status
Key fields:
Field	Meaning
phase	Pod state (Running)
Ready	Pod ready
restartCount	container restart count
podIP	Pod network IP
________________________________________
6️⃣ Check Resource Usage of Pods
View CPU and memory usage:
oc adm top pods -A --sum
Example output:
CPU: 505m
Memory: 8982Mi
--sum gives total cluster usage.
________________________________________
7️⃣ Check Pods in etcd Namespace
oc get pods -n openshift-etcd --show-labels
Example:
etcd-master01
installer-1-master01
installer-2-master01
________________________________________
8️⃣ Check Container Resource Usage
oc adm top pods etcd-master01 -n openshift-etcd --containers
Example:
etcd            44m    269Mi
etcd-metrics     8m     30Mi
Shows CPU and memory per container.
________________________________________
9️⃣ List All Monitoring Resources
oc get all -n openshift-monitoring
Shows:
•	pods
•	services
•	deployments
•	replica sets
Example pods:
alertmanager-main
cluster-monitoring-operator
kube-state-metrics
________________________________________
🔟 View Pod Logs
Example:
oc logs alertmanager-main-0 -n openshift-monitoring
Used to debug:
•	configuration loading
•	errors
•	startup issues
________________________________________
1️⃣1️⃣ Check Cluster Events
oc get events -n openshift-kube-controller-manager
Events show:
•	pod creation
•	leader election
•	image pulling
•	errors
Example:
LeaderElection
Pulled
Started
________________________________________
1️⃣2️⃣ Check Node Status
oc get nodes
Example:
master01   Ready   control-plane,master,worker
Healthy node status:
Ready
________________________________________
1️⃣3️⃣ Check Node Resource Usage
oc adm top node
Example:
CPU: 719m
Memory: 12069Mi
Shows node utilization.
________________________________________
1️⃣4️⃣ Check Node Capacity
CPU capacity:
oc get node master01 -o jsonpath='{.status.capacity.cpu}'
Allocatable CPU:
oc get node master01 -o jsonpath='{.status.allocatable.cpu}'
Example:
Capacity: 6
Allocatable: 5500m
________________________________________
1️⃣5️⃣ Check Max Pods per Node
oc get node master01 -o jsonpath='{.status.allocatable.pods}'
Example:
250
________________________________________
1️⃣6️⃣ Inspect Node Resources
oc describe node master01
Shows:
•	CPU requests
•	memory requests
•	limits
•	events
Example:
cpu requests: 2809m (51%)
memory requests: 12359Mi (83%)
________________________________________
1️⃣7️⃣ Check Node Service Logs
View CRI-O container runtime logs:
oc adm node-logs master01 -u crio --tail 1
View kubelet logs:
oc adm node-logs master01 -u kubelet --tail 2
Important services:
Service	Purpose
kubelet	manages containers
crio	container runtime
________________________________________
1️⃣8️⃣ Debug a Node
oc debug node/master01
Then access host:
chroot /host
Check kubelet:
systemctl status kubelet
Check crio:
systemctl is-active crio
Exit:
exit
exit
________________________________________
1️⃣9️⃣ Collect Cluster Debug Data
Run must-gather:
oc adm must-gather --dest-dir /home/student/must-gather
This collects:
•	cluster configuration
•	logs
•	events
•	operator states
Used when opening Red Hat support cases.
________________________________________
2️⃣0️⃣ Inspect Logs from must-gather
Example:
tail -5 ~/must-gather/.../gather.logs
Shows errors like:
secrets "support" not found
server doesn't have resource type "clusters"
________________________________________
2️⃣1️⃣ Inspect Specific Operator
oc adm inspect clusteroperator/openshift-apiserver \
--dest-dir /home/student/inspect \
--since 5m
Collects debugging data only for last 5 minutes.
________________________________________
2️⃣2️⃣ View Operator Configuration
Example:
cat ~/inspect/.../cluster.yaml
Shows:
•	API server configuration
•	annotations
•	conditions
________________________________________
2️⃣3️⃣ Clean Up
Delete debugging data:
rm -rf must-gather inspect
________________________________________
2️⃣4️⃣ Finish Lab
lab finish cli-health
________________________________________
🔑 Key Commands Summary
Task	Command
Check operators	oc get clusteroperators
Operator details	oc describe clusteroperators
List pods	oc get pods
Pod logs	oc logs <pod>
Pod resource usage	oc adm top pods
Node status	oc get nodes
Node resource usage	oc adm top node
Node logs	oc adm node-logs
Debug node	oc debug node/<node>
Cluster diagnostics	oc adm must-gather
Inspect resources	oc adm inspect
